OPTION WHEEL, vertical mode gotchas:
  - trackHeight MUST be >= cardHeight + 2 * visible * step. Get it wrong and
    the outer cards spill out of the track and land on the controls. That
    happened on the first attempt.
  - per-card rotation has to be zero when stacked. The 6deg-per-step tilt that
    works in the horizontal fan reads as scattered cards vertically.
  - the axis swap is on --ow-x / --ow-y only; spreadX stays the per-step
    distance along whichever axis is active.

VIOLET LEADERSHIP CARDS: theme.text.secondary and accent.violet.text both
read as low-contrast grey on that gradient. They use literal white /
violet-200 / slate-100 now. Same class of trap as the Eagle Scout chip —
check a token against its actual background rather than assuming.

BEAM/PHOTO REGRESSION TEST: compare FULL 2D rectangle intersection, not just
horizontal extents. At mobile widths the hero columns stack, so the photo sits
below the rays and a horizontal-only check reports a false positive. Verified
clean at 1440/900/700/420/380.

